      <!-- EC-003: Operational transparency & trust -->
      <details id="EC-003">
        <summary><span class="badge medium" style="color: var(--slate);">MEDIUM</span> Operational Transparency &amp; Trust &mdash; Editorial Policy Absent, Support Discoverability Scattered <span style="font-size: 12px; color: var(--text-secondary); font-weight: 400;">(EC-003)</span></summary>
        <div class="finding-content">
          <p style="margin-bottom: 12px;">The basic trust scaffolding (Privacy, Terms, Support) is in place. What's missing is the editorial-integrity layer AI models increasingly weight for YMYL-adjacent content: a named editorial policy, content standards, or fact-checking guidelines. For a company publishing hundreds of blog posts about brand management and AI, the absence of this surface weakens the argument that Marq's published content is authoritative.</p>

          <details style="margin-top: 12px;">
            <summary style="font-weight: 500; font-size: 14px;">What we found</summary>
            <div class="finding-content">
              <p style="margin-bottom: 12px;">Coverage 75%, mean content quality 3.00, schema completeness 0%. Three of four expected pages Present; Editorial Policy is Absent.</p>

              <div style="margin-top: 12px; font-size: 13px;">
                <strong>Per-page scoring</strong>
                <ul style="margin-top: 6px; line-height: 1.7;">
