  <!-- Entity Identity & Proof Structure Topic Group -->
  <div class="findings-section">
    <h3>Entity Identity &amp; Proof Structure</h3>
    <p class="topic-intro">Schema markup doesn't just help AI understand your content (that's the Understand layer). It also makes verifiable claims about your business: who you are, what you build, what customers prove about you. When those claims are incomplete or disjoint across pages, AI agents lose confidence in the whole site. This section evaluates whether Marq's structured data builds trust or undermines it.</p>

    <!-- HIGH: Capability Surface Disjoint From Brand Identity -->
    <details id="BV-003">
      <summary><span class="badge high">HIGH</span> Capability Surface Is Disjoint From the Brand Identity <span style="font-size: 12px; color: var(--text-secondary); font-weight: 400;">(BV-003)</span></summary>
      <div class="finding-content">
        <p style="margin-bottom: 12px;">Trust in the agentic era depends on a machine being able to say "this brand, this capability, same entity." For Marq that means being able to prove, in structured form, that www.marq.com and developers.marq.com are the same company. Today they are not linked in either direction: no Organization sameAs entry on the brand home, no reciprocal sameAs on the developer portal, no shared @id, no 301 bridge. An AI agent reading both sites independently will treat them as two companies with confusingly similar names.</p>

        <details style="margin-top: 12px;">
          <summary style="font-weight: 500; font-size: 14px;">What we found</summary>
          <div class="finding-content">
            <p style="margin-bottom: 12px;">Three reinforcing breaks in the entity-identity chain:</p>
            <ul style="margin: 0 0 12px 24px; line-height: 1.8;">
              <li>The Organization schema on www.marq.com lists six sameAs links (social + Crunchbase). It does not list developers.marq.com.</li>
              <li>The Organization schema on developers.marq.com does not reciprocate with a sameAs link back to www.marq.com.</li>
              <li>Neither site uses an explicit @id to declare "these two Organization nodes are the same entity."</li>
            </ul>
            <p style="margin-bottom: 12px;">This is the TRUST-layer expression of BV-001. In FIND the problem is "agents can't reach the capability." In TRUST the problem is "agents can't verify the capability belongs to Marq." Same root, different failure mode.</p>

            <p style="margin-bottom: 12px; padding: 12px; background-color: var(--cream); border-left: 3px solid var(--accent-copper); border-radius: 4px; font-style: italic; color: var(--text-secondary);"><strong>Recommendation:</strong> Redacted for this sanitized sample.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
      </div>
    </details>

